 [('Explain “latency” to a beginner.','Explique.','It’s the delay before something starts to load.'),('Switch register.','Mude.','Among engineers: p95 latency. With clients: how long users wait.'),('Avoid condescension.','Evite.','Let me explain it with an example.')],
 ('Write a 6-sentence blog paragraph explaining a technical term to a non-expert.','Last week a friend asked what an API is. I almost said “a programmatic interface exposing endpoints”. Instead I said: “It’s a waiter. You tell it what you want, and it fetches it from the kitchen.” She laughed and understood at once. Jargon saves time among engineers, but it builds walls elsewhere. The skill is code-switching without talking down.',['Explicação simples','Evitei jargão'],'6 frases'),
